WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:11.220
The history of gaming extends 5,000 years into the past to ancient Egypt.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.720
Ancient games foretold the futures of men and kings.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.200
They were magic ceremonies that determined a person's fate.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.340
These ceremonies were known as the "Shadow Games."

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.990
In the present, a young boy solves the Millennium Puzzle.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.210
He becomes the heir to the Shadow Games.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.300
This boy possesses two hearts - one of light and one of darkness.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.210
He is known as "Yu-Gi-Oh."

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.340
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.250
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.000
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:10.700
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.800
You're on the other side of the table

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.170
I'm talking to you, but...

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.100
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.350
Even though I'm this close to you

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:39.620
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:46.360
What is truly precious?

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:55.640
The Power of Friendship!
Lava Battleguard and Swamp Battleguard

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.760
Mokuba!

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.000
Mokuba!

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.250
Mokuba, where are you?

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.770
I can't find Mokuba anywhere.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.040
They must have taken him to Pegasus's castle.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.240
The only way to get into Pegasus's castle is to collect ten Star Chips.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.490
Yeah.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.720
I found some cards!

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:26.350
Those are mine.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:29.770
You also play Duel Monsters, Honda?

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.440
Sure.  I was interested, so I bought a few cards.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.670
I figured I'd bring them with me.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:38.770
What's this?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.940
What is it, Jonouchi?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.440
Battleguard?  I have something similar.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.180
Here it is.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.200
Lava and Swamp Battleguards.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.760
They should stick together.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.520
It's inconvenient for me, but I'm willing to take this card off your hands.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.480
I never said I'm giving it to you!

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:03.200
Come on.  It's useless if you keep it.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.160
Fine.  I'll loan it to you for a little while.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.770
Sheesh...  You two should be called the Lava and Swamp Dummies.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.800
Yugi!

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.170
Sorry.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.810
My Harpies attack.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.730
Triangle Ecstasy Spark.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.200
I win.  Leave your Star Chips and get out of here.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.650
Damn!

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.330
Dueling has lost its thrill.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.120
I can't stand it!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.690
I can't believe I lost to him!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:59.130
I finally found you, Mai Kujaku.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.240
It's me, Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.530
How dare you make a fool out of me on the ship!

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.450
Get out, loser!

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.240
Oh, I remember now.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.760
Battle me again right here!

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.120
I'm not interested in men who I've already defeated.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.530
Buzz off.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:25.910
I took second in the national championships.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:29.770
And I've already got five Star Chips.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.290
Eight Star Chips?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:39.280
I only need two more to enter Pegasus's castle.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.320
And I've already decided who I'm getting those remaining Star Chips from.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.330
Yugi, huh?  I'll defeat him.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.860
Yugi won't lose to you-

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.040
I have an idea.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.090
Fine, I'll duel you.  But on one condition.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:04.160
Those kids don't look that tough, so they may be perfect for you, Jonouchi.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:04.720
What?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.800
Now hold on.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.440
Weevil looked pretty weak, but he turned out to be really strong.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.120
You're right.  But when you think about it, there's probably no one weaker than Jonouchi on this island.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.900
You're right.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.360
What's with you guys!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.610
Quit taking shots at me!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.500
That shrill voice can only belong to...

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.540
We meet again, Jonouchi.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.400
Mai Kujaku!

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.000
You're all sticking together as usual.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.400
Were you ducks in a previous life?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.210
Ducks?

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.880
Yugi, isn't he actually an annoyance?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:48.430
If Jonouchi wasn't holding you back, you'd already be at Pegasus's castle.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:49.850
That's not true.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.000
Oh, I'm not here to battle you.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.600
I'm here for...

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.130
Jonouchi!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:03.110
You won last time, but my servant will defeat you this time!

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:04.530
Servant?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.000
It's been a while, Yugi and Jonouchi.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.720
Dinosaur Ryuzaki.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.820
You're Mai's servant?

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.720
I'm a little jealous.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.280
Stop being stupid!

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.400
Hurry up and decline.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.520
Oh my, are you scared?

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.040
Fine!  I accept!

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.160
Jonouchi!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.480
What are you thinking?

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.930
Don't do it!  There's no way you can win!

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.160
He's an easy target.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.130
I'll have to thank Mai.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.680
I want to get revenge personally, but that would be immature.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:47.190
If I defeat Ryuzaki after he's beaten Jonouchi, that'll make up for my loss.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:51.400
She's only doing this because Jonouchi defeated her.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.240
But just watch.  Yugi will help him like last time and win-

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.530
By the way.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.360
I have one condition in this duel.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:03.330
The peanut gallery can't give any advice to the duelists.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.200
It's not a real duel if you're getting advice, right Jonouchi?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.230
No way!  That's-

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:13.330
I accept those terms.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.400
I may be nuts.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:20.550
If I lose my Star Chips in this duel, I'll be thrown off the island.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.600
But I want to win using my own skills.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:27.560
I don't want to rely on Yugi forever.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.320
Are you serious?

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:33.560
Someone who finished 8th in the regionals can't defeat the runner-up in the nationals!

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.440
Sorry.  He lost his cool.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:39.070
Forget that he said that he'd accept your duel.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:41.090
This is none of your business!

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.330
What are you doing, you jerk?

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.660
What she said was right.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.400
If it weren't for me, Yugi would already be at the castle.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.320
Jonouchi, I don't feel the same.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.800
If I can't take care of myself, it's better if I lose now.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.200
Listen to yourself.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.170
If you lose, what will happen to your sister?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:12.940
That's enough, you two!

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.040
I'm done cheering for this idiot!

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.080
Honda!

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:22.450
Leave him alone, Yugi!

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.480
What a farce.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.130
What did you say?

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.640
What are you going to do?

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:31.790
If you beg, I'm willing to call off the duel.

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.680
Of course I accept.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.000
Yugi, don't give me any advice in this duel.  Got it?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.730
Okay...

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:42.850
All right!  Duel, standby!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.290
You can do it, Jonouchi.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:00.450
Without Yugi's advice, I feel super nervous.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:08.010
Hey servant!  If you don't win, you don't get the prize!

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.530
What's she giving you if you win?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.530
That's a secret.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.840
How many Star Chips are you wagering?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.880
Two!  That's all my Star Chips!

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:25.550
Fine.  My section of the field is Wasteland and yours is Sogen grassland.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:32.340
Ryuzaki, your Dinosaur cards led you to finish 2nd in the nationals, so they must be powerful.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:36.890
But I also have a strong combo that I used to beat Mai.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:43.360
With my special move, Time Wizard turns Baby Dragon into the mighty Thousand Dragon.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.600
Let's go!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:55.730
Duel!

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.480
Anzu, keep an eye on Jonouchi.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.410
I'll be right back.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:04.880
Yugi!

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:12.650
I'm lucky!  I drew Time Wizard and Baby Dragon from the start!

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.050
Yugi?

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.990
It's fine.  I'll still win this duel without Yugi.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:21.970
Here I go!

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:25.170
Baby Dragon in defense position!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.920
Go ahead and play your monster.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.230
I'll use my special combo to defeat you next turn.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:39.570
I play my card Two-Headed King Rex in attack position.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:49.210
King Rex destroys Baby Dragon in a single attack.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:51.240
My Baby Dragon!

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:52.560
You fool.

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:56.700
Only a fool would show their monster in defense position.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.240
Use your head.

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:01.560
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.930
You're doing horribly!

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.480
You're such an amateur.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:13.120
There goes his plan to use Time Wizard to turn Baby Dragon into Thousand Dragon.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.200
Hurry up and play your next card!

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.960
No matter what card you play, my Dinosaur card will stomp it!

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:46.930
His monster looks tough, but I have strong cards in my hand too.

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.290
Go, Leogun!  Defeat King Rex!

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.480
You fool.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:05.010
The Wasteland Field Power Source has powered up my King Rex.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.280
Oh no!  I forgot!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.290
Dinosaur Foot Stomp!

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.530
Damn.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.600
My real goal is to defeat Mai Kujaku.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.890
I'll finish Jonouchi as fast as possible.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:23.120
That's it for me.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:25.280
Hurry up and play your next card.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.470
My field is Sogen.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:31.160
It benefits Warrior and Beast-Warrior Type monsters, which I have a lot of.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.330
I'll play this card.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:38.650
The Field Power Source powers up my Axe Raider!

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:41.210
Gale Slice!

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.550
I play this card.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:49.370
Sword Arm of Dragon!

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.890
Dragon Tail Sword!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.690
I really can't win?

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:08.640
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:10.880
Pull yourself together already!

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.130
Yugi.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:17.890
That idiot.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.240
Are you okay, Honda?

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:25.720
Yugi, why are you here?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:31.090
I promised I wouldn't give any advice, so I didn't need to stay there.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:34.720
Yugi, what kind of nonsense is that?

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:38.410
It doesn't matter if I'm there or not, but it's different for you.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.480
You don't need to keep that promise.

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:44.100
You'll be meddling in, but isn't that what friendship is all about?

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:48.610
I won't say anything to Jonouchi until the duel is over.

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:49.840
Yugi!

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:56.850
Jonouchi believes that if he wins on his own, then Shizuka can also beat her illness.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.930
But still...

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:05.410
Jonouchi forced himself to battle.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:09.000
Watching him to the end proves our friendship.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.090
Jonouchi will understand how you feel, Honda.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:15.210
Yugi.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.250
Damn, where's Yugi?

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:26.080
How pathetic.  I'm still depending on Yugi.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.880
I'll win on my own.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.490
That's what I decided for Shizuka's sake.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:36.290
I don't have any cards in my hand that can stand up to his Dinosaurs.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.420
This is Time Wizard.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:44.880
But other than creating Thousand Dragon, I don't know how to use it.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.630
What other powers does it have?

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.940
I'll set this on the field for now.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:55.440
That card is likely Time Wizard.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:56.760
Servant!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:01.180
I know.  That must be Time Wizard.

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:06.370
An amateur like him can never use that card to its full potential.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.600
Time Wizard is an incredibly powerful card.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:15.360
That card defeated my Harpie Ladies.

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:20.130
I play a monster in defense position.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.080
No matter what card it is, I'll destroy it.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.570
Megazowler!

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.690
Megazowler's Charge Attack!

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:42.290
You may as well give up.

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.130
I play this card!

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.320
You finally play a decent card.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:55.860
But Flame Swordsman and Megazowler have the same number of attack points.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:58.930
Megazowler!  Charge Attack!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.040
Ryuzaki, you fool!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:05.370
Flaming Battle Sword!

00:16:15.090 --> 00:16:18.090
What?  My Megazowler!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.400
I won.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:25.440
Flame Swordsman is Fire Attribute, which is strong against Dinosaur cards.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.410
But I'm sure he was just lucky.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:31.420
Your turn, you dino punk!

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:35.610
Flame Swordsman's sword has Fire Attribute, so that's problematic.

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:37.180
I switch this to defense position.

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.890
Go, Flame Swordsman!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:48.410
He's strong!  Jonouchi can win!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.480
Damn!  All I can do is defend!

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.530
Things are now going my way.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:01.340
Don't underestimate me.

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:05.210
I still have a number of rare cards in my deck.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.760
All right!  Come out!

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.690
Serpent Night Dragon!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:23.200
This premier card was only given to those who passed the second round of the national tournament.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:27.460
Jonouchi, you'll never own this card!

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:31.450
Go!  Nightmare Shadow Sonic!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.170
My Flame Swordsman.

00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.440
Jonouchi!

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:43.850
Do I have any cards that can defeat a monster that powerful?

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.290
I got this from Honda.

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:59.080
You must be an idiot to challenge us to a fight all alone.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:03.060
It annoys me when people gang up to pick on a weakling.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.330
We'll make sure that you can never stand up again!

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:09.200
Jonouchi!

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.490
Get him!

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:27.080
Are you okay, Jonouchi?

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:29.460
You're so reckless!

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:32.520
I never asked for your help.

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:33.960
What?

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:35.840
This was my fight.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.000
I could've beaten them by myself.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.210
I don't need your help!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.530
Since I was a hothead, I never realized that...

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.250
Honda...

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:52.600
Whenever I got into trouble, you were by my side.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.850
What are you doing, Jonouchi?

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.060
Pull yourself together!

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:58.550
Honda!  Yugi!

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:02.890
That fool can't do anything without me.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.130
All right, Honda.  Let's battle together!

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:13.400
That's mine!

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:18.370
That's pointless.  Finish him with Nightmare Shadow Sonic!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:22.070
Attack Swamp Battleguard!

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:38.560
What?  He reflected back my Shadow Sonic?

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.600
My Lava Battleguard!

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.600
Honda's card saved me.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:52.630
I get it.  When those two monsters are together, their abilities help each other.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:56.290
Honda, your friendship saved Jonouchi.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.890
Thank you, Honda.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.520
Damn.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.200
All right!  I'll keep going!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:17.010
Let's battle together, Jonouchi!

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:19.400
Whatever.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.850
Celebrate while you still can.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:36.320
Jonouchi survived his pinch with the power of friendship.

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.540
But that was only for an instant.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:41.840
Dinosaur Ryuzaki's most powerful monster appears, so Jonouchi is in a pinch once again!

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.880
Jonouchi, realize that there's a way to turn the tables!

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:47.720
And an unexpected person shows up.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:51.340
Bakura?  You're actually here?

00:20:51.340 --> 00:20:55.440
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Black Flame!  Red-Eyes B. Dragon

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.290
Duel, standby!

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:09.960
The flask glistens

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:17.810
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:26.780
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:34.550
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:40.380
Shower of happiness

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:44.500
I will shower you with it

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:52.780
I will support your lonely back

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:57.010
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:01.140
You are not alone

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:07.860
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
